<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>On-policy derivation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive on-policy BoN objective in greater detail.
We will start from the following form of policy gradient with <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\max</annotation></semantics></math>(<a href="#A4.E11" title="In Appendix D On-policy derivation ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\max\!\left(\left(r\!\left(y_{j},x\right)\right)_{j\in I}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.309em;" width="0.309em"><mi>r</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\max\!\left(\left(r\!\left(y_{j},x\right)\right)_{j\in I}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here we can replace sum over all subsets with sum over all possible <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math> values:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\\
\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)\end{subarray}}1\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\\
\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)\end{subarray}}1\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that all completions are sorted by their scores in the ascending order.
In that case, <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subseteq[j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subseteq[j]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given that, we can simplify the summation:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k,j\geq i\end{subarray}}1\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k,j\geq i\end{subarray}}1\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce <math id="A4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">With this notation, we get the form of policy gradient from <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.2 On-policy case ‣ 3 Pass@k optimization ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>
Since <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of <math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-s over subset, <math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is just equal to the size of that subset:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{ij}=\bigl|\{I\subseteq[j]\ :\ |I|=k,\ i\in I,\ j\in I\}\bigr|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">:</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\bigl|\{I\subseteq[j]\ :\ |I|=k,\ i\in I,\ j\in I\}\bigr|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Consider two cases for <math id="A4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=i</annotation></semantics></math> we need to find total number of subsets of size <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with elements up to <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and containing <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\binom{i-1}{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\binom{i-1}{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise – we are choosing <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-1</annotation></semantics></math> elements to pair with <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> we similarly need to find total number of subsets of size <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with elements up to <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and containing both <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\begin{cases}\binom{j-2}{k-2},\quad j\geq k,\,j&gt;i,\\
0,\quad\text{otherwise}\end{cases}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\begin{cases}\binom{j-2}{k-2},\quad j\geq k,\,j&gt;i,\\
0,\quad\text{otherwise}\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">here we are selecting <math id="A4.I1.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k-2</annotation></semantics></math> elements to add to <math id="A4.I1.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I1.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Off-policy derivation</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The approximation of unbiased off-policy derivation takes the form of:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{j\in I}\delta_{j}\right)\max\!\left(\left(r(y_{j},x)\right)_{j\in I}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{j\in I}\delta_{j}\right)\max\!\left(\left(r(y_{j},x)\right)_{j\in I}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly to on-policy case, we can replace sum over all subsets with sum over all possible <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math> values:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\\
\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[n],i\in I\\
|I|=k\\
\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that all completions are sorted their scores in the ascending order.
In that case, <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left(r(y_{l},x)\right)_{l\in I}=r(y_{j},x)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subseteq[j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subseteq[j]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given that, we can simplify the summation:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k,j\geq i\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=1}^{n}r(y_{j},x)\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k,j\geq i\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite this similarly to on-policy case with <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> coefficients:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=i}^{n}w^{\prime}_{ij}\,r(y_{j},x)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\binom{n}{k}}\,\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\nabla_{\theta}\!\log\pi(y_{i}\mid x)\,\sum_{j=i}^{n}w^{\prime}_{ij}\,r(y_{j},x)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{ij}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{ij}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[j],i,j\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Consider two cases for <math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In case of <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=i</annotation></semantics></math> we get:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{ii}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[i],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{ii}=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}I\subseteq[i],i\in I\\
|I|=k\end{subarray}}\left(1+\sum_{l\in I}\delta_{l}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, then the sum is over empty set and is equal to <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Otherwise, we can regroup summed deltas.
In the sum <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in every term, therefore it will counted <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{i-1}{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{i-1}{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> times (total number of subsets of size <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a maximum element).
All other deltas appear in the sum <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{i-2}{k-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{i-2}{k-2}</annotation></semantics></math> – number of subsets that contains both <math id="A5.I1.i1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and any particular element before it.
Combining everything we get:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{ii}=\begin{cases}\binom{i-1}{k-1}(1+\delta_{i})+\binom{i-2}{k-2}\sum\limits_{l&lt;i}\delta_{l},\quad i\geq k\\
0,\quad i&lt;k\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{ii}=\begin{cases}\binom{i-1}{k-1}(1+\delta_{i})+\binom{i-2}{k-2}\sum\limits_{l&lt;i}\delta_{l},\quad i\geq k\\
0,\quad i&lt;k\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In case of <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> we can similarly group deltas in the summation.
Since <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> always contains <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+\delta_{i}+\delta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+\delta_{i}+\delta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in every term and will be counted <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{j-2}{k-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{j-2}{k-2}</annotation></semantics></math> times (total number of subsets of size <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> being the maximum element).
All other deltas appear in the sum <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{i-3}{k-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{i-3}{k-3}</annotation></semantics></math> – number of subsets that contains both <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math> and any particular element before them.
Combining everything we get:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}_{ij}=\begin{cases}\binom{j-2}{k-2}(1+\delta_{i}+\delta_{j})+\binom{j-3}{k-3}\sum\limits_{l&lt;j,l\neq i}\delta_{l},\quad j\geq k,\,j&gt;i,\\
0,\quad\text{otherwise}\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}_{ij}=\begin{cases}\binom{j-2}{k-2}(1+\delta_{i}+\delta_{j})+\binom{j-3}{k-3}\sum\limits_{l&lt;j,l\neq i}\delta_{l},\quad j\geq k,\,j&gt;i,\\
0,\quad\text{otherwise}\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Full evaluation results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present full evaluation results for CodeContests in Table <a href="#A6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>; for LiveCodeBench in Table <a href="#A6.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>; for LiveBench in Table <a href="#A6.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>; for CodeForces in Table <a href="#A6.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>; for MBPP in Table <a href="#A6.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> and Table <a href="#A6.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ Appendix F Full evaluation results ‣ The Best of N Worlds:Aligning Reinforcement Learning with Best-of-N Sampling via max@k Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
